From a06e53f8e021c18c7bdffc6f5682bbfb664fbdbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parker Lavering <plavering@live.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 12:36:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 29/34] perf(daemon): parallelize compactorGetRowCounts to fix
 N+1 query pattern
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Serial loop issued one COUNT(*) per table after listing tables — 41+
round-trips for a 40-table DB. Dispatch all COUNT queries concurrently
via goroutine-per-table with sync.WaitGroup + Mutex + error channel.
Wall-clock time drops from Σ(query_i) to max(query_i).

information_schema.table_rows is not used because callers compare pre/post
counts as a data-loss integrity gate; approximate statistics would either
false-alarm or mask real row loss. COUNT(*) is preserved; only the
execution order changes.

Adds rows.Err() check on the table-listing cursor (missed previously).

Adds compactor_dog_rowcounts_test.go with a fake database/sql driver
covering: empty DB, single/multiple tables, list error, count error,
parallel execution timing assertion, exact-count regression guard, and
an end-to-end integrity gate simulation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
